 "samples": [
  "One day, a little girl named Lily found a needle in the garden. She wanted to fix the needle, so she pushed the needle very gently with her hand.\nLily's little brother, Tom, saw her trying to fix the needle. Tom knew that his arm would help him fix the needle. Tom said, \"Don't worry, Tom! I will fix the needle.\" Tom went to Mia and told her not to do it. Mia was still upset, but she knew Tom was good.\nTogether, Lily and Tom cleaned the needle. They were both happy and thanked Tom for his help. They played with the cloth all day long. And from that day on, the needle became more careful with the needle, and they never forgot playing with it again.",
  "Once upon a time, there was a little car named Beep. Beep lived on a road and were friends. One day, Beep went for a ride in the yard.\nAs Beep went down the road, he met a big dog. The dog said, \"Hello, Beep!\" But Beep wanted to play with the dog, but he didn't know how to make him happy. He kept playing on the road and thought about how much fun he was.\nWhen he got to the dog's home, something unexpected happened. The dog started to talk! Beep was a dog! The dog was surprised and said, \"Hi, Beep! I am a big dog!\" Beep and the dog became friends and played together every day. And they all lived happily ever after.",
  "One day, a little fish named Fin was swimming near the river. Fin was scared. He did not know what to do. But his friend, Fin, saw him and asked Fin to help him. Fin wanted to help the fish.\nFin and Fin swam together. They swam fast and jumped, but Fin was too fast. Fin felt sad. He wished he could swim and play with Fin. Fin wished he could swim with Fin, and they all swam together.\nFin learned that being brave is better than having friends. He was happy that he could help his friends and swim fast. And they all lived happily ever after.",
  "Once upon a time, in a land full of trees, there were pretty flowers, flowers, and sweet flowers. One day, a little bird came to the land. The bird saw the flowers and wanted to eat them.\nThe bird flew away, and the little bird saw the beautiful flowers. It had many colors and was filled with happy, but then it had a bad ending. The sun was gone, and it was a bad ending to a big day."
 ],
